WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.677
This is App.

2
00:00:01.727 --> 00:00:05.384
The goal: three screens you can walk, including a way back.

3
00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:09.415
An app can be a few screens, connected by buttons.

4
00:00:09.765 --> 00:00:11.583
A button press is an event.

5
00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:15.163
It runs one instruction: go to the screen you chose.

6
00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:19.441
The person supplies the tap. The computer runs the program.

7
00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:24.028
Here's the reference app. Screen 1: What is lauhala?

8
00:00:24.078 --> 00:00:27.056
Button A, How to coil, goes to screen 2.

9
00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:29.751
Screen 2: How the rose is made.

10
00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.730
Button A, See the rose, goes to screen 3.

11
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.337
Button B, Back, goes to screen 1.

12
00:00:35.687 --> 00:00:37.683
Screen 3: Finished rose.

13
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.702
Button A, Start over, goes to screen 1.

14
00:00:41.552 --> 00:00:44.906
Now, the editor. Leave Editing screen on 1.

15
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:51.386
Before you type, the preview says Untitled screen, and This screen has no explanation yet.

16
00:00:51.936 --> 00:00:54.646
Type a title, and a short explanation.

17
00:00:54.696 --> 00:00:56.786
The preview updates as you type.

18
00:00:57.336 --> 00:01:00.391
Next, label Button A, and choose where it goes.

19
00:01:00.441 --> 00:01:02.945
Here, How to coil goes to screen 2.

20
00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:08.457
Button A starts out pointing at screen 1, so check where it goes on every screen.

21
00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:11.169
Now change Editing screen to 2.

22
00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:16.025
The boxes show that screen's own words, and the preview moves to screen 2.

23
00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.507
Fill in screen 2 the same way, then screen 3.

24
00:01:20.057 --> 00:01:23.323
Button B is optional. Use it for a way back.

25
00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:26.201
On screen 2, Back goes to screen 1.

26
00:01:26.551 --> 00:01:28.871
Copying the reference app is allowed.

27
00:01:29.721 --> 00:01:30.842
Now walk it.

28
00:01:30.892 --> 00:01:37.320
Tap the buttons in the preview: screen 1, screen 2, screen 3, then back to screen 1.

29
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.642
The line under the preview tells you where you are.

30
00:01:41.192 --> 00:01:43.780
The preview uses your destinations.

31
00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.794
There's no hidden Next order.

32
00:01:46.344 --> 00:01:50.955
So if Button A on screen 2 points at screen 2, the preview stays put.

33
00:01:51.305 --> 00:01:55.200
That's a bug. To repair it, point Button A at screen 3.

34
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.622
Then press Reset the walk.

35
00:01:57.672 --> 00:02:01.307
It clears the walk, and the preview goes back to screen 1.

36
00:02:01.857 --> 00:02:05.206
Walk it again: 1, 2, 3, and back to 1.

37
00:02:06.056 --> 00:02:09.857
Last, write one sentence about a connection, or a repair.

38
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:11.690
Make the sentence yours.

39
00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.211
Now you try.

40
00:02:13.261 --> 00:02:16.560
Which connection, or which repair, will you write about?

41
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.902
Pause, and write it in your own words.

42
00:02:22.852 --> 00:02:24.516
Then press Check the app.

43
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:26.633
A tap is the event.

44
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:30.462
It runs one instruction: go to the screen you chose.
